# Week 2 review: tactics without labels
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | calm, warm chess coach","b":"gemini:Puck | eager club player, relaxed and good-humoured; never exaggerated"}
prompt: "Can you find the tactic when the theme is not named? Can you win material from a position against the computer?"
next: {"title":"What should you play as White?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/chess-30-days/15-what-should-you-play-as-white.cast"}

## Warm-up: solve first, name it after
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 6r1/pp4pp/4k3/8/8/7P/PP4P1/5BK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Bc4+, Ke5, Bxg8]}
      - {fen: 1q3r1k/pp4pp/7N/3Q4/8/8/PP3PPP/6K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qg8+, Rxg8, Nf7#]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title Warm-up

A: Week two, reviewed: can you find the tactic when nobody tells you its name? Two warm-ups first.
    draw position

B: No label? Then I don't even know which pattern to look for.
    highlight piece_g8

A: Don't hunt for a pattern. Ask the Three Questions, checks first.
    highlight piece_e6

    pause 0.3

    ask "Win material." widget chess line true hints ["Which checks do you have?","Your bishop on f1."] themes ["skewer"] voice a
        right: Bishop to c4, check. The king has to step off the diagonal, and the bishop takes the rook behind it.
        wrong: Look at every check first. What stands behind the king?

B: A skewer. I only knew its name afterwards.
    highlight piece_g8

A: Solve first, name it afterwards. Second one.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

B: My knight on h6 is attacked. I'd save it.
    highlight piece_h6

A: Checks first, even one that gives your queen away.
    highlight piece_d5

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["Checks first, even a queen sacrifice.","Your knight guards g8."] themes ["smothered mate","mating pattern"] voice a
        right: Queen to g8, check! The knight guards g8, so the rook on f8 must take, and knight to f7 is mate: the king is smothered by its own pieces.
        wrong: Look at every check, even one that gives your queen away. What could take her on g8?

B: Smothered mate. And I wanted to save the knight.
    point at.ref piece_h8 gesture circle

A: A name helps you remember a pattern. Finding one in a game takes something else: today's lesson.
    highlight piece_f7

## Find the target first
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 1nb2rk1/pp4pp/5p2/3q4/8/1P1B4/P3QPPP/1N3RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Nc3, Qe5]}
      - {fen: 1nb2rk1/pp4pp/5p2/3q4/8/1P1B4/P3QPPP/1N3RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Bc4, Be6, Bxd5, Bxd5], arrows: [{from: d5, to: g8}]}
      - {fen: 5rk1/ppq2ppp/1b3n2/6B1/8/3Q4/PP3PPP/1B2R1K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qxh7+, Nxh7]}
      - {fen: 5rk1/ppq2ppp/1b3n2/6B1/8/3Q4/PP3PPP/1B2R1K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Bxf6, g6]}
      - {fen: 4r1k1/p2q1ppp/1p6/3n4/8/5Q1P/PP1B1PP1/4R1K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rxe8+, Qxe8, Qxd5]}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0
    safety: 0

    card title "Find the target first"

A: In a game, nobody names the tactic for you. So what do you look for?
    draw position

    pause 0.6

B: Nothing hangs here, so I'd just develop. Knight to c3, and it hits her queen.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 2.5

A: She steps away, and you've just missed winning her.
    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.6

B: How? Nothing was loose.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

A: True: no piece hangs. But a loose piece is only one kind of target.
    animate safety 1 duration 1

    animate safety 0 duration 0.5

A: Look at the lines: her queen and her king stand on one diagonal.
    draw arrow_0

    erase arrow_0

    pause 0.3

    ask "Win material." widget chess line true hints ["Queen and king on one diagonal.","Your bishop on d3."] themes ["pin"] voice a
        right: Bishop to c4 pins the queen to her king. Black blocks with his bishop, but the queen is still attacked: bishop takes queen, bishop takes back. A queen for a bishop.
        wrong: Which of your pieces can attack the queen along that diagonal?

B: A pin. Once I saw the line, I didn't need the name.
    highlight piece_g8

A: The second kind of target: the king. White to move.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

B: Queen takes h7, check! The bishop backs her up.
    animate plies_shown 1 duration 1.6

A: And the knight takes her. Before you go for the king, ask who guards the square.
    animate plies_shown 2 duration 1.6

    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

B: The knight on f6.
    highlight piece_f6

A: Then the guard is your target.
    highlight piece_f6

A: The king is the target; the guard is the way in.
    highlight piece_g8

    pause 0.3

    ask "Win material." widget chess line true hints ["Take away the guard of h7.","Your bishop on g5."] themes ["removing the defender"] voice a
        right: Bishop takes the knight. Now queen takes h7 would be mate, so Black blocks with g6, and the knight is gone for nothing.
        wrong: Who guards h7? Take that piece first.

B: Take the guard, and the mate threat does the rest.
    point at.ref piece_h7 gesture circle

A: Last one. Before any move, name the target. Which kind of target is here? Pick one.
    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    quiz "Which kind of target is here? Pick one." on_canvas true say_question false buttons_at.x 910 buttons_at.y 414 buttons_layout column voice a
        right: A guard with two jobs: Black's queen on d7 guards the rook on e8 and the knight on d5.
        wrong: Who guards the rook, and who guards the knight?
        * Loose piece
        * Two on a line
        + Guard with two jobs

A: So make the guard choose.
    highlight piece_d7

    pause 0.3

    ask "Win material." widget chess line true hints ["Give the queen a job she must do now.","A capture with check on e8."] themes ["overloading"] voice a
        right: Rook takes e8, check. The queen has to take back, and the knight on d5 has lost its only guard: queen takes it.
        wrong: Make her take on e8 first. What does she stop guarding?

    erase position

B: Loose pieces, the king, two on a line, a guard with two jobs.
    text w_loose "loose" x 500 y 520 font_size 56
    text w_king "king" x 500 y 435 font_size 56
    text w_line "line" x 500 y 350 font_size 56
    text w_guard "guard" x 500 y 265 font_size 56

A: Find a target first, and the Three Questions find the move.
    highlight w_loose w_king w_line w_guard

## Your turn: the week-two test
feedback:
    style: dry
    perfect: Four for four. The patterns are yours now.
    good: Most of them. The misses are your training list.
    poor: Two weeks is short. The misses come back until they stick.
    none: The test will wait for you.
use: chess_board
with:
    positions:
      - {fen: 5rk1/pb1q1p1p/1p4p1/8/4N3/8/PPQ2PPP/5RK1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Nf6+, Kh8, Nxd7]}
      - {fen: 2N2rk1/5ppp/8/8/1Q2b3/8/q4PPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Qxf8+, Kxf8, Rd8#]}
      - {fen: r2q2k1/pp3ppp/8/8/8/2b5/PP2QPPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1, moves: [Rxd8+, Rxd8, bxc3]}
      - {fen: r2q1bk1/p4ppp/1p6/8/8/2N1Q3/PPP3PP/R5K1 b - - 0 1, moves: [Bc5, Qxc5, bxc5], flip: true}
      - {fen: r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/5n2/8/1bP5/5N2/PP3PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 1}
    position_shown: 0
    plies_shown: 0

    card title "Your turn"

A: You've seen how a target gives the tactic away. Your turn: four positions, no names, and a score at the end.
    draw position

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["Look for two big targets one knight jump apart.","Your knight on e4, with check."] themes ["fork"] voice a test week2
        right: Knight to f6, check: it hits the king and the queen on d7. The king steps aside, and the queen falls.
        wrong: Which check also attacks something big?

A: Next one, still White.
    animate position_shown 1 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["His king has no escape square on the back rank.","Only the rook on f8 guards it."] themes ["back rank","decoy"] voice a test week2
        right: Queen takes f8, check! The king has to take back, and rook to d8 is mate: the knight covers e7.
        wrong: Rook to d8 is met by the rook on f8. Can you remove that guard with check?

A: Black's bishop has just taken your knight on c3.
    animate position_shown 2 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["Checks before recaptures.","The d-file is open now."] themes ["in-between move"] voice a test week2
        right: Rook takes d8, check, before anything else. The rook takes back, and only then does the pawn take the bishop: a queen and a bishop for a rook.
        wrong: The bishop can wait one move. What did his capture open?

A: Last one: Black to move, so the board turns.
    animate position_shown 3 plies_shown 0 duration 0.4

    pause 0.3

    ask "Find the best move." widget chess line true hints ["White's queen and king stand on one diagonal.","Your bishop on f8."] themes ["pin"] voice a test week2
        right: Bishop to c5 pins the queen to the king. Whatever White does, the queen is lost for the bishop: queen takes, pawn takes back.
        wrong: Look for a line with the king at the end of it.

    erase position

A: You scored {week2.score} of {week2.total}.
    results test week2

B: And the ones I missed?
    text review "Review" x 500 y 400 font_size 64

A: They come back now, with any you missed on earlier days.
    explore activity review_misses

    erase review

    animate position_shown 4 plies_shown 0 duration 0.1

A: Back to White, against the computer. Nobody names the tactic here.
    draw position

A: Find the target, and win at least a piece within five moves.
    explore activity vs_computer goal.kind win_material goal.amount 3 goal.within 5 store wm

    erase position

A: Tactics have names, but in a game you hunt targets: loose pieces, the king, lines, and busy guards.
    text w_loose "loose" x 500 y 520 font_size 56
    text w_king "king" x 500 y 435 font_size 56
    text w_line "line" x 500 y 350 font_size 56
    text w_guard "guard" x 500 y 265 font_size 56

A: Homework: one slow game today, fifteen plus ten or slower. Then find its first mistake.
    erase w_loose w_king w_line w_guard

